  "gitHistory": [
    {
      "commit": "d6df8395ef108bc6d2f58606e02f77d83e369390",
      "record": "d6df8395ef108bc6d2f58606e02f77d83e369390\n2026-07-07T20:33:36-07:00\nURRenderKit Tier 3: BoardPainter + CGContextRasterizer; UrBoardView reroute\n\nFactor the board's draw commands out of `UrBoardView.body` into a backend-agnostic\n`BoardPainter` rendering against a SwiftUI-free `PaintTarget`, in a new Liquid-Glass-FREE\n`URRenderKit` library (UrKit + CoreGraphics/Accelerate only \u2014 compiles under\nUR_CI_ENGINE_ONLY / Xcode 16, so its board-parity laws can run in CI).\n\n  \u2022 URRenderKit: UrBoardState/HeroStone/StoneColor + BoardPhase (moved down; UrUI\n    re-exports via @_exported import), BoardGeometry (palette + trackPoint topology),\n    PaintTarget (6 primitives \u2014 fill/stroke/translate/scale/rotate/blur; semantic paths\n    so each backend builds native shapes), BoardPainter (faithful port), and a headless\n    CGContextRasterizer (sRGB, deterministic vImage box blur, premultiplied source-over).\n  \u2022 UrUI: GraphicsContextTarget \u2014 the one SwiftUI-touching adapter \u2014 maps the primitives\n    onto GraphicsContext with the identical Path/Color constructors the prototype used.\n    UrBoardView becomes a thin shell; its TimelineView only supplies the BoardPhase.\n  \u2022 URRender: `--board-ir` (ImageRenderer, frozen phase) and `--board-cg` (the CG path,\n    no run-loop) dev renders.\n\nOn-screen output is BYTE-IDENTICAL after the reroute (isolated board, reduceMotion,\nvia ImageRenderer \u2014 same SHA before/after). The board now also renders through Core\nGraphics, deterministically, with no ImageRenderer and no run-loop.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>"
    },
    {
      "commit": "8fabff9e01026551d46dc6d4465182fdb4db2ab3",
      "record": "8fabff9e01026551d46dc6d4465182fdb4db2ab3\n2026-07-07T20:42:25-07:00\nURRenderKit settle gate: R1/R3/R4/R5/R6 (CI-visible, pure Core Graphics)\n\nAdd URRenderSettleTests \u2014 the oracle-bound board-parity gate \u2014 plus PixelKit (raw-buffer\nSHA-256 + amber/teal channel classifier). All five laws are pure Core Graphics (no\nImageRenderer, no SwiftUI), so the test target is unconditional and runs under\nUR_CI_ENGINE_ONLY on Xcode 16 \u2014 the board's pixels get CI coverage on every push.\n\n  \u2022 R1 determinism \u2014 same (state, phase) \u21d2 byte-identical buffer (SHA-256).\n  \u2022 R3 fit invariance \u2014 k\u00d7 scale \u21d2 k\u00d7 pixels; board centered in an oversized slot.\n  \u2022 R4 state\u2192pixel presence \u2014 target bloom, suggested amber rim, and litPath teal all\n    appear at their trackPoint coordinates.\n  \u2022 R5 two-color law \u2014 the best-move cue classifies AMBER (not teal); the engine spine\n    classifies TEAL (not amber) \u2014 the rule becomes a pixel test, not prose.\n  \u2022 R6 idle/reduce-motion canonical \u2014 the reduceMotion phase is clock-independent, so\n    two clocks render byte-identically.\n\nDeterminism fix: `rgbaBytes()` now returns PACKED rows (drop the CG row-stride padding,\nwhich vImage leaves uninitialized) so the hash is stable across runs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>"
    },
    {
      "commit": "e839809b91f146dcda92af9afd401b501d06a997",
      "record": "e839809b91f146dcda92af9afd401b501d06a997\n2026-07-07T20:56:09-07:00\nURRenderKit R2: CG\u2194ImageRenderer board parity (confinement form, local-only)\n\nAdd URRenderParityTests \u2014 the acceptance gate for retiring ImageRenderer on the board\npath. Renders the same board through both backends and proves they are the same scene in\nspatial-confinement form (NOT a whole-frame \u22642/255 claim):\n\n  \u2022 Solid, non-rosette interiors agree \u22643/255 worst-case, \u226599.9% within \u22642/255 (the\n    material-policy bound); whole-frame mean abs error 0.69/255.\n  \u2022 Every larger disagreement is confined to the DECLARED-SOFT set \u2014 AA edges, blur halos,\n    translucent glows (IR alpha<255, the render's own coverage) and the five rotated\n    gold-gradient rosettes (known BoardGeometry.rosettes) \u2014 never a structural mismatch.\n    The residual is exactly where any two rasterizers differ: antialiasing, Gaussian blur,\n    and 1-LSB gradient sampling (SwiftUI vs CGGradient).\n\nBoth backends rasterize into the SAME explicit sRGB CGContext via ImageRenderer's\nrender(rasterizationScale:renderer:) closure \u2014 no display-P3/nsImage tag mismatch, and no\nTimelineView (BoardCanvas at a frozen phase) so no run-loop hazard. Local-only (needs\nSwiftUI + ImageRenderer); the pure-CG laws R1/R3/R4/R5/R6 remain CI-visible.\n\nBoardRender gains a public `init(context:)` so the same PixelKit sampling serves both\nbackends.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>"
    },
